    "line": 14,
    "summary": "subtitleStyle is imported from checkout-theme but never used in the file",
    "failure_scenario": "Dead import re-authored by the restyle; every reader/grep of subtitleStyle hits a false usage and lint noise. Simpler form: drop it from the import list (chipStyle/labelStyle/etc. are all real uses; this one has zero references beyond line 14)."
  },
  {
    "file": "client/src/pages/checkout.tsx",
    "line": 200,
    "summary": "quoteStep is stored state kept in sync with quote.viewedAt via a useEffect when it is derivable at render time",
    "failure_scenario": "State + sync-effect (lines 200, 206-208) for a value computable as `quote?.viewedAt ? 'confirm' : localAdvance` — the effect adds an extra render pass and a second source of truth that can disagree with the server flag. Simpler form: keep only a boolean `advanced` set by the button click and derive `step = advanced || quote?.viewedAt ? 'confirm' : 'view'`. (Side note for the correctness angles: the real quote GET sets viewedAt on the very first fetch and returns it, so this effect appears to skip step 1 entirely outside mock mode.)"
  },
  {
    "file": "client/src/pages/checkout.tsx",
    "line": 1257,
    "summary": "the spin @keyframes rule is now duplicated four times across the two customer pages instead of living once in the shared checkout.css",
    "failure_scenario": "Identical `@keyframes spin` strings at checkout.tsx:1257 and :1665 plus split-payment.tsx:164/385 (const at :390), each injected via inline <style>; four copies to keep in sync and repeated DOM style nodes. Simpler form: one `@keyframes spin` in client/src/styles/checkout.css, which both files already import."
  },
  {
    "file": "client/src/pages/checkout.tsx",
    "line": 1245,
    "summary": "the quote branch rebuilds the page wrapper and duplicates the 'Secured by Windcave' footer verbatim instead of sharing a shell helper",
    "failure_scenario": "Lines 1245-1258 re-create pageStyle wrapper + maxWidth div + footer that also exist in the main return (footer identical at 1254 vs 1657-1660) and in renderTerminal; a wording or style tweak must now be made in two or three places. Simpler form: extend renderTerminal into a `renderPage(children)` helper that owns wrapper + footer, used by all three."
  },
  {
    "file": "client/src/pages/split-payment.tsx",
    "line": 269,
    "summary": "first-person and subsequent-payer branches re-author near-identical edit-amount blocks and confirm/pay button pairs differing only in state variable names",
    "failure_scenario": "The input+error+'use equal split' block (269-283 vs 345-360) and the editMode?confirm:pay footer (each ~15 lines) are copy-paste with editValue/subEditValue, confirmedCustom/subConfirmed, maxEditAmount/remaining swapped — ~60 duplicated lines where a validation or style fix must be applied twice. Simpler form: one AmountEditor fragment (value, max, onConfirm, onCancel) + one confirm/pay footer helper parameterized by the active pair."
  }
]
```

Out-of-scope observation (one sentence, for the correctness angles): the server's quote GET marks the quote viewed and returns `viewedAt` set on the customer's *first* fetch, so the `quote?.viewedAt → setQuoteStep("confirm")` effect at checkout.tsx:206 appears to skip the "view quote" step entirely against the real backend (mock returns `viewedAt: null`, which is why screenshots showed step 1).
